# Lenovo Legion Y700 Gen 4, TB322FC, codename elden (SM8750, Snapdragon 8 Elite).
# Not the TB323FU: that one is SM8850 (8 Elite Gen 5, "canoe", Adreno 840),
# a different chip this kernel doesn't run on.
# Sourced by kernel-common/build.sh and kernel-common/cmdline.sh.
#
# Source: h0cheung's Linux 7.2.8 tree for the tablet
# (github.com/h0cheung/tb322fc-linux-kernel), which already carries the
# SM8750 platform and board support, the unaligned atomics emulation and the
# ath12k scan fix. On top: the 8 Elite fixes of ours it doesn't have.
# Pin bf96c3d4 (2026-10-20, history rebased since 5134673b): carries the GMU
# HFI/devcoredump fixes and the SSBS-on-sigreturn fix that were our 0008 and
# 0009, so those two are gone from kernel-elden/patches.
# Config: the same ROCKNIX SM8750 config as the Odin 3 (drivers as modules,
# firmware from the rootfs), plus the tablet's drivers (steamos.config).
#
# Lenovo's ABL boots a plain header v4 boot.img and passes its own Android
# cmdline and DTB, so the kernel carries the DTB and the cmdline built in.

source "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../kernel-sm8750/soc.env"

KNAME=elden
KVER=7.2.8
KSRC_URL=https://github.com/h0cheung/tb322fc-linux-kernel/archive/bf96c3d4048973298ede78487177c6f1b4f6bc0f.tar.gz
PORT_DIRS="kernel-elden"
# The tree is the platform support: no ROCKNIX SM8750 patches or trees.
PATCH_DIRS=""
PATCH_SKIP=""
SKIP_ROCKNIX_DTS=1
KEEP_IMAGE=1
DTBS="sm8750-lenovo-elden"

# GPU microcode from linux-firmware; the zap shader is signed for the tablet
# and comes from its own firmware on the rootfs.
BUILTIN_FW="
lfw/qcom/gen80000_gmu.bin:qcom/gen80000_gmu.bin:1ad8175e6cd01ea76c64d20b83600038c52dd29844b48d57b11b769b038863a5
lfw/qcom/gen80000_sqe.fw:qcom/gen80000_sqe.fw:30ee3301534f95799d4afaf73864f3c369baa5a5dea8481e7f0cb8cc941f396c
lfw/qcom/gen80000_aqe.fw:qcom/gen80000_aqe.fw:67562ad5baae3a133c92a6e48a9d1b1a9a867fe2f85b49324e244e963f3b89c5
"

# The kernel's own cmdline (CMDLINE_BUILTIN). The tablet is installed with
# fastboot: our boot.img in the active boot slot and the system with /home in
# Android's userdata partition (scripts/mk-elden-flash-images.sh); Android's
# super stays, the firmware is copied out of it. There is no FAT partition, so
# the boot log goes to /var/log/steamos-arm-boot and debug-logs to /boot on
# the root.
# From the tablet's validated cmdline: the ABL leaves clocks, power domains
# and regulators to Linux only partly set up, so nothing unused is turned off
# at late init, and fw_devlink is permissive.
CMDLINE_BUILTIN=1
CMDLINE_ROOT=PARTLABEL=userdata
CMDLINE_SOC="firmware_class.path=/var/lib/steamos-arm/firmware/elden console=tty0 irqaffinity=0-1 cgroup.memory=nokmem,nosocket nosoftlockup mem_sleep_default=s2idle efi=noruntime usbcore.autosuspend=-1 fw_devlink=permissive arm-smmu.disable_bypass=0 clk_ignore_unused pd_ignore_unused regulator_ignore_unused initcall_blacklist=clk_disable_unused,regulator_init_complete,genpd_power_off_unused"
# The video decoder's firmware (qcom/vpu/vpu35_p4.mbn) is signed for the
# tablet and not in its Android image, so qcom_iris fails every open with
# "core init failed" and leaves the core powered: don't load it.
CMDLINE_SOC="$CMDLINE_SOC module_blacklist=qcom_iris"
# The tree's SSBS-on-sigreturn fix (Proton/Wine signal frames carry no SSBS bit)
# is on by default only for the Oryon X1 MIDR; force it on for the 8 Elite.
CMDLINE_SOC="$CMDLINE_SOC ssbd_sigreturn=1"
# Beta: kernel and systemd messages on the panel in a font readable at 3K, so
# a photo shows where a boot stops, and the debug log collector on every boot.
CMDLINE_QUIET=0
CMDLINE_SOC="$CMDLINE_SOC fbcon=font:TER16x32 steamos.debug=1"
